{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he went up onto the mountain.</b> To the top of the mountain, and immediately the pericope of Behar was stated, which speaks of the laws of the land, in order to draw their hearts — that as reward for accepting the Torah they would inherit the land." "<b>Forty days and forty nights.</b> From dawn of the seventh of Sivan until dawn of the seventeenth of Tammuz. The order of the pericope of Mishpatim is complete."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "The phrase 'שלימא סדרא דפרשת משפטים' appears to be a colophon marking the completion of the seder/reading cycle for Mishpatim; translated literally as 'the order of the pericope of Mishpatim is complete.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:17.368138466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}